Lesson: Don't go to that narrow corridor to wait for the giants.
Wait for them come to you where you have more room to move and push the
boulders to the lava. For example, one favorite place for me to wait in
the Valkyrie Quest bottom level is where one giant is shown on the first
line I included in the quote. I wait for a giant to move to the spot West
of that, kill the giant and push the boulder. It normally sinks without a
trace, but I guess it may fill one square of lava, in which case I make
the next square West my place for waiting..
And if a giant gets South of me, I still can just push the remaining
boulder that way.

And like Janis said, squeezing through the boulders is one way to move
them. You'll just to iterate West and East until you have enough room, and
stripping down in the Quest may feel scary..

